      "side": 1,
      "message": "(1) Nice that this booting with less cpus isn\u0027t a problem and nicely covered by the cpus_to_visit mask.\n\n(2) An smp platform (with capacity-dmips-mhz\u003d1024 for all cpus), otherwise this code wouldn\u0027t be active at all) with an energy model and therefore no SD_ASYM_CAPACITY flag would at least have an SD_SHARE_CAP_STATES flag set (on MC or DIE) so this would be covered as well. topology_detect_flags() returns 1 in this case as well. \n\nEven though we normally want to use the energy model for asymmetric capacity systems, like real big.Little and gold-silver (different cpu_scale values due to different max freq values).",
